{
  "text": "Lots of small food sellers still run on paper. A home baker. A market stall. The menu is a printed sheet, and there's no website. AI assistants are starting to shop for people, but they can't see a paper menu. In one US survey, nearly half of food and lodging businesses had no website. Shelfie gives them a shop that AI can buy from.",
